    "status": "in_review",
    "title": "Georgia HB 463 (2026): flat income tax rate to 4.99%",
    "url": "https://gov.georgia.gov/press-releases/2026-05-11/gov-kemp-signs-legislation-lowering-taxes-and-supporting-economic-growth",
    "date": "2026-07-15",
    "author": "PolicyEngine",
    "description": "Georgia HB 463 (2026), signed May 11, 2026, sets the state flat individual income tax rate at 4.99% for tax year 2026 \u2014 0.10 percentage points below the previously scheduled 5.09% and 0.20 percentage points below the 2025 rate \u2014 and creates temporary AGI exclusions of up to $1,750 each for tips and overtime pay (2026-2028). Impacts on this page measure the 2026 rate acceleration against the prior-law 5.09% schedule using PolicyEngine Georgia data. Measured against the 2025 rate instead, the year-over-year reduction is roughly twice as large; external estimates of that framing are $778M (Governor OPB) and $797-948M (GBPI/ITEP). The tips and overtime exclusions are not scored due to a microdata imputation gap.",
    "key_findings": [
      "Reduces government revenue by $0.3 billion in 2026 (PolicyEngine policyengine-us-data, policyengine-us 1.772.0)",
      "11.4% of households gain; 0.0% lose",
      "No measurable change in overall poverty (SPM)"
    ],
